    "notes": "XLSX: 4 title/branding rows precede the header (skip_rows=4); sheet 'Current_Victorian_Licences_By_L'; 465 data rows, 21 columns incl. two pairs of empty spacer columns. Sheet subtitle states 'Current Victorian Liquor Licences as of 31/08/2026' - a snapshot date, not per-record; observed_at falls back to dataset metadata. Nothing in the data changes per record over time, so address columns need no validity dates. No ABN/ACN column: Licence Number is 8-digit (ABN checksum 0%, ACN checksum 9.2% = chance) - deliberately unmapped. entity_type unmapped (no column states legal entity type). REVISION 3: adopts the reviewer's approved scope unchanged (premises address only; ALL postal columns unmapped) and adds ONLY the placeholder handling: '[Not applicable] -' in Suburb (7 rows, shape '[a a] -') is upper-cased and gated out at address.locality; the same '[NOT APPLICABLE] -' placeholder is nulled in address.full and the '0' postcodes in address.postcode so no placeholder value can be emitted.\n\n[ext-v1] Holdout fixes: (1) 'NOT APPLICABLE' was reaching ext.establishment.lga as data - added as a null_if placeholder there and on the other text fields (Region, Metro/Regional, capacity). (2) Removed the Licence Category -> ext.entity.industry_code crosswalk rule after the critic showed an unreviewed AI table producing division-level ANZSIC codes contradicted by the data; industry code is now unmapped with that reason. (3) Removed Trading Hours -> ext.licence.condition because ~136 rows duplicate the category string, making the condition claim redundant. Premises address/locality/postcode moved to the establishment role via base_rule_edits; Postal* columns remain the subject's correspondence_address. Known and accepted: 7 rows have postcode '0' and 7 have '[Not applicable] -' suburbs, so the establishment address triple can be blank while other premises attributes (region) are still emitted - those columns are independently populated by the publisher. Licence status, entity_type and legal_form are not inferred; no ABN/ACN column exists in this file.",
